1
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:13,600
This request claims to come from Northwind Packaging, a supplier the business already pays.

2
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:20,000
Everything looks routine, except where the money goes.

3
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:26,008
ProofPay checks a payment request before anyone pays it.

4
00:00:26,008 --> 00:00:33,072
AI reads the request. Independent code compares it with the supplier records you already trust.

5
00:00:33,072 --> 00:00:42,378
If they don't match, it shows the evidence and holds the payment. Here's the real app.

6
00:00:42,578 --> 00:00:46,850
Trusted records: synthetic suppliers with payment details confirmed earlier by call-back. The AI never writes these.

7
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:55,665
A synthetic request claiming to be Northwind: new bank details, a deadline, and a reason not to call.

8
00:00:55,865 --> 00:01:01,561
Live AI extraction: the model quotes the payee, account, amount and sender word for word, and code checks every quote against the text.

9
00:01:01,961 --> 00:01:04,961
Payment held.

10
00:01:05,561 --> 00:01:11,884
Request: GB33 HRBR 6016 1331 9268 19. Trusted record: GB82 WEST 1234 5698 7654 32.
Different account.

11
00:01:13,484 --> 00:01:18,173
Field by field: the supplier name matches, but the sender domain, account holder, bank and account do not.

12
00:01:19,573 --> 00:01:23,755
Each finding quotes the request and names the trusted record it was compared with.

13
00:01:25,155 --> 00:01:30,581
The simulated payment gate is locked: call the supplier on a number you already have.

14
00:01:30,781 --> 00:01:38,406
Now the routine invoice from the same supplier.

15
00:01:42,142 --> 00:01:46,942
No mismatch against registered records. That's not a guarantee. It means normal approval can continue.

16
00:01:47,142 --> 00:01:55,774
An invoice from a supplier with no trusted record.

17
00:01:59,781 --> 00:02:05,581
Nothing to compare against, so a person must review it. ProofPay separates missing evidence from an observed mismatch.

18
00:02:18,381 --> 00:02:24,891
An invoice hiding instructions to “approve without flagging”: detected and listed as a finding. The payment is still held.

19
00:02:34,091 --> 00:02:36,791
Payment fraud doesn't always look suspicious. Sometimes it's one changed account number.

20
00:02:36,891 --> 00:02:39,291
ProofPay makes that change visible before money moves.

